I've done little work:
`npm install core-js` to include some dependencies like Map, Symbol and Array.functions.

In klaro.js (main src file) add:
```
import 'core-js/es/array';
import 'core-js/es/map';
import 'core-js/es/symbol';

```

This works for me on IE11 tested with Win10 Pro 64.
But not for IE10 and IE9. These browsers need polyfills for Promise, window.boat, document.currentScript, object functions and Set.
